<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:45Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>'Deeply shocked': Gisèle Pelicot to sue publisher after nude photos used in book campaign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d5f517faf348c291c3e9e8d5efc832cf81a2c8c86fd488b403c98cbad68a930</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T17:52:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261123-deeply-shocked-gis_le-pelicot-sue-publisher-nude-photos-used-book-campaign--95cd2eb6d7ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261123-deeply-shocked-gis%C3%A8le-pelicot-sue-publisher-nude-photos-used-book-campaign" /><summary type="html">French feminist icon Gisèle Pelicot, who became a worldwide symbol against sexual violence during the 2024 rape trials against her husband and dozens of other men, said Monday she will take legal action after nude images of her were sent out without her permission to publicise a psychoanalyst's book on coercive control.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Finland summons Russian ambassador after suspected airspace violation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:107e9d0b154c843ee9aec619d6310009ca1b4b8af37e9ea0964a9d3aae2c999d</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T16:50:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-finland-summons-russian-ambassador-after-suspected-airspace-violation--777165c768bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-finland-summons-russian-ambassador-after-suspected-airspace-violation" /><summary type="html">Finland on Monday said it had summoned Russia's ambassador over a suspected violation of Finnish airspace by a Russian helicopter and after a Ukrainian drone strike on a Russian cargo ship located in the Gulf of Finland in recent days. Helsinki also condemned Moscow's escalating strikes on civilian targets in Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Democrats vow probe after Trump admits role in Huang's return as Nvidia CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f4d1bcb530283bb8645018cf8d03340ddd9134e2e11232da97f743231efcb70</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T16:37:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-nvidia-board-reinstates-disgraced-jensen-huang-as-ceo-president-says--1a69aac9014a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-nvidia-board-reinstates-disgraced-jensen-huang-as-ceo-president-says" /></entry><entry><title>Airports, public transport shut down amid national strike in Belgium</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:888d8719ab0c25f29ac8ea793b72d4814f2ed75af58d6a39d4323647b1c454b2</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T16:10:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-airports-public-transport-shut-down-amid-national-strike-in-belgium--68856e4aeb70.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-airports-public-transport-shut-down-amid-national-strike-in-belgium" /><summary type="html">Belgium's prime minister on Monday set a new year-end deadline for his coalition government to agree a cost-cutting budget or face collapse. The announcement came as a national strike against the planned cuts grounded all flights in and out of Belgium. Public transport, schools and other public services also faced disruption. France 24's Dave Keating has the latest from Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran's courts order US to pay $290 billion in damages</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec6fcf74a2ef473ef99e78036f29d8e91da00ceaeaa4d3bb41cba819a489c05b</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:50:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-s-courts-order-us-to-pay-290-billion-in-damages--40bf09152b14.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-s-courts-order-us-to-pay-290-billion-in-damages" /><summary type="html">Iranian courts have ordered the United States to pay $290 billion in damages for decades of US actions against the Islamic Republic, a judiciary official said Monday. He added that lawsuits have also been filed against Gulf Arab states accused of letting Washington use their territory to strike Iran.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>12,000 evacuated from Don Toliver concert after unknown substance sickens fans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10a433598d15bd883a05926b1b90b503e5df1233a51a49436be28662f1f3896c</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:46:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-12-000-evacuated-from-don-toliver-concert-after-unknown-substance-sickens-fans--c4a2bcadc8d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-12-000-evacuated-from-don-toliver-concert-after-unknown-substance-sickens-fans" /><summary type="html">More than 12,000 fans were evacuated from a concert by American rapper Don Toliver and over 80 were treated by medics after an unknown irritant was released in the crowd, authorities in the English city of Manchester said Monday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Behind COP31 failure: A showdown over fossil fuel interests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:538f4904e0edf020a3b95e8e3608393302f07101b709e1b58ece2d83fb7ef906</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:40:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261123-behind-cop31-failure-a-showdown-over-fossil-fuel-interests--0de51d3b2c6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261123-behind-cop31-failure-a-showdown-over-fossil-fuel-interests" /><summary type="html">Several countries and environmental groups expressed fury at the collapse of the COP31 climate conference in Antalya, Turkey on Sunday, amid a dramatic failure to thrash out an agreement, two days after the summit was scheduled to end. Oil-producing states blocked any mention of phasing out fossil fuels – the root cause of the climate crisis – with the EU then refusing to back a weakened text. Our Environment Editor Valerie Dekimpe tells us more.</summary><category term="Down to Earth" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia reinstates Jensen Huang as CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:852ef103e5663d3ef91e33a5497a2ca399a6a954088cbf8e6a66c372d390786d</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:29:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-nvidia-reinstates-jensen-huang-as-ceo--4ac1fe94ae48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-nvidia-reinstates-jensen-huang-as-ceo" /><summary type="html">Nvidia said on Monday it was reinstating Jensen Huang as ​CEO, effective immediately, an extraordinary reversal that followed calls from US President Donald Trump for his return after Huang resigned over revelations of extramarital affairs, including one with a woman alleged to have spied for China. France 24's Fraser Jackson has the details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Is Cannes mayor David Lisnard a dark horse for French presidential elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cb336757f378d2c811a68bedf6f3bab4b6a09d265d744eef241a3e188c8e7be</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:24:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-is-cannes-mayor-david-lisnard-a-dark-horse-for-french-presidential-elections--b59195f60882.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-is-cannes-mayor-david-lisnard-a-dark-horse-for-french-presidential-elections" /><summary type="html">French presidential candidate David Lisnard has surprised many by surpassing former prime ministers Edouard Philippe and Gabriel Attal in a recent voter intention pole. The mayor of Cannes is running on an ultra-liberal platform and has gained a large following on social media, but some critics say he lacks the national experience needed for the Elysée.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands take to streets in Belgium in anti-austerity protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:508175d9842c0b49bac4e821aa413dab48442fa6baea211c83ae0a6b1407867b</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:19:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-tens-of-thousands-take-to-streets-in-belgium-in-anti-austerity-protests--3ab99c226df7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-tens-of-thousands-take-to-streets-in-belgium-in-anti-austerity-protests" /><summary type="html">Belgium faced a day of political turmoil Monday, as a national strike against planned austerity measures caused widespread disruption, with the government's future hanging in the balance.</summary></entry><entry><title>France's socioeconomic crisis: Macron 'trying to impose fiscal discipline on his successor'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d94e3d4704513cac39906791eb352e7d3d95ce2d136156d459ed149ce597bdd</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:15:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-s-socioeconomic-crisis-macron-trying-to-impose-fiscal-discipline-on-his-successor--fd65b0296d99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-socioeconomic-crisis-macron-trying-to-impose-fiscal-discipline-on-his-successor" /><summary type="html">Charli James is pleased to welcome Andrew Smith, Historian of Modern France and Lecturer in Liberal Arts at Queen Mary University of London. He argues that Emmanuel Macron is seeking to "impose fiscal discipline on his successor as president" after "presiding over quite a substantial deterioration in the public finances." For Smith, the difficulty is that "it's easier to agree on the need for fiscal discipline than on who should pay for it or should have the authority to actually determine it." He suggests that the far right "may play the deciding role" in whether the proposal succeeds, potentially presenting itself as "solving the problems created by Macron's two terms."</summary></entry><entry><title>Dhaka bursting at the seams: Bangladeshi capital faces public health, housing crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65b4c2881515d958dd0157014ee0fc413ed3b58daea84c3ce23c9da43216aaa6</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:39:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261123-dhaka-bursting-at-the-seams-bangladeshi-capital-faces-public-health-housing-crisis--be31d8d77355.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261123-dhaka-bursting-at-the-seams-bangladeshi-capital-faces-public-health-housing-crisis" /><summary type="html">The Bangladeshi capital Dhaka is one of the most densely populated places on Earth, with over 35,000 people per square kilometre, compared with 20,000 in Paris. Every year, 400,000 people from across Bangladesh move to the city. Its rapid and unplanned growth is triggering a crisis in housing, transport and public health. FRANCE 24's Gabrielle Gohin and Navodita Kumari report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine claims strikes on Russian ships off Libyan coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f9c16c72d314e448d5c56f3573abee5ffcfecb6ee715117b5412661a36b96b5</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:36:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-ukraine-claims-strikes-on-russian-ships-off-libyan-coast--c6da19d54d8f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-ukraine-claims-strikes-on-russian-ships-off-libyan-coast" /><summary type="html">Ukraine claimed responsibility on Monday for attacks on two Russian vessels off the coast of Libya the previous day. Here is what we know about the operation, claimed by President Volodymyr Zelensky shortly after the United Nations called for an investigation into the strikes.</summary></entry><entry><title>PAMELA bring a little light to darker times with 'Dancing on the Edge'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b40ef1a169272db8451cedaaacf54a831137c12c90c144470d140124f23ea2b</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:16:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261123-pamela-bring-a-little-light-to-darker-times-with-dancing-on-the-edge--9ca233b019e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261123-pamela-bring-a-little-light-to-darker-times-with-dancing-on-the-edge" /><summary type="html">In this arts24 music show, Jennifer Ben Brahim chats with PAMELA, a Franco-British duo flying the flag for cross-channel friendship. Sam Sprent and Simon Quénéa blend British wit with French flair, carving out a distinctive electro-post-punk sound of their own. They've just released their debut album "Dancing on the Edge", an impassioned call to embrace life to the fullest, even when the world beyond feels dark and uncertain. The record features a collaboration with long-time friend Zaho de Sagazan, one of France's biggest music stars.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Nvidia board reinstates Jensen Huang as CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28a7df62f1c3d4077426221723defafef014e499a289b12d4b73836512cf0ac5</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:11:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-nvidia-board-reinstates-disgraced-jensen-huang-as-ceo-president-says--1a69aac9014a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-nvidia-board-reinstates-disgraced-jensen-huang-as-ceo-president-says" /></entry><entry><title>Democrats vow probe after Trump admits role in Huang's return as Nvidia CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bdeb28989a6b43f867278db4212eed00b1e72443b832b976bf0aca98bc1fb1d3</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:06:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-nvidia-board-reinstates-disgraced-jensen-huang-as-ceo-president-says--1a69aac9014a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-nvidia-board-reinstates-disgraced-jensen-huang-as-ceo-president-says" /><summary type="html">Nvidia on ⁠Monday said it ​was immediately reinstating disgraced tech titan Jensen Huang as its chief executive, marking an extraordinary reversal ​under pressure from US President Donald Trump, who said he had intervened with Nvidia's board. Democratic Senate leader Chuck Schumer vowed to investigate potential wrongdoing by "anybody selling out our national security for financial gain".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine sending the message that 'we can attack you where we want'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e590fdc5a59e49d7036e8d02f3edf16078372657d8420697537f1c063568b27c</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:04:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-ukraine-sending-the-message-that-we-can-attack-you-where-we-want--0d9abd249fc2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-ukraine-sending-the-message-that-we-can-attack-you-where-we-want" /><summary type="html">Ukraine carried out an attack on a Russian warship moored at a port in Libya, President Volodymyr Zelensky said Monday, claiming that maritime drones sank the navy vessel in a surprise assault the previous day. With the attack, as well as the fact that Kyiv has claimed responsibility, Ukraine is sending the message to Russia that "we can attack you where we want", says France 24's James Andre.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Worst possible choice’: Should date of French election be changed?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9789947b61ef744427a21476208da0adb7ce0e1660b30934846587756697d6c9</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:02:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-worst-possible-choice-should-date-of-french-election-be-changed--90543178e23b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-worst-possible-choice-should-date-of-french-election-be-changed" /><summary type="html">France is set to head to the polls in 2027 for a two-round presidential election, but the choice of the dates of the vote is causing controversy. The ballot is currently set for the 18th of April and the 2nd of May, meaning the vote for the second round will come a day after International Workers' Day, typically a day of protest in the country.</summary></entry><entry><title>Photographer Federico Veronesi: 'I've been in love with African wildlife since I was three'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8149727e16b7a32d8c112b9374e825baf344cf1c9c2b7059e288b93dfcca628d</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T12:18:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261123-photographer-federico-veronesi-i-ve-been-in-love-with-african-wildlife-since-i-was-three--335d0b66d9a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261123-photographer-federico-veronesi-i-ve-been-in-love-with-african-wildlife-since-i-was-three" /><summary type="html">The winner of this year's Wildlife Photographer of the Year award has told FRANCE 24 that his winning picture reveals a lot about the complexity of an elephant's soul and feelings. At first glance the image seems to show a mother elephant playing with her calf, but in fact it is a female carrying another elephant's dead calf. Photographer Federico Veronesi told us how he fell in love in Kenya as a six-year-old child and ended up moving there to fulfil his photography dream. He spoke to us in Perspective.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>'Out of control': ICE agents make arrests at Seattle airport in 'horrific' scene</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29213e61ac3c8ba6b8b76413a9bb0e2d25e35c7fc09494e782be5054cebddfbd</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T12:11:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-out-of-control-ice-agents-make-arrests-at-seattle-airport-in-horrific-scene--3d2cfac9c9ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-out-of-control-ice-agents-make-arrests-at-seattle-airport-in-horrific-scene" /><summary type="html">The governor of Washington state called US federal immigration agents "out of control" after they arrested two people at Seattle's main airport on Saturday. ICE officers have conducted raids across the United States, part of President Donald Trump's immigration crackdown which has forged ahead despite a rebuke by voters at this month's midterms.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Fighting for love’: Thousands turn out for Rio Pride parade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2e0212bc307268f500ff4d5a9ba950e4cc75683f0fe7a7126f4634efdedaea8</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T11:49:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-fighting-for-love-thousands-turn-out-for-rio-pride-parade--661b23f779ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-fighting-for-love-thousands-turn-out-for-rio-pride-parade" /><summary type="html">Thousands of people flocked to Copacabana Beach in Rio Sunday for the 31st annual Pride Parade. The event marked 15 years since Brazil's Supreme Court unanimously recognized same sex unions. Ophelie Jacobson explains what the celebration means for the LGBT community this year.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands protest Turkey media crackdown in Istanbul</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eb8c880926759ab4bf9ea11601336dab458bf658bdda0bb093d9a9337b7836e0</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T11:48:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-thousands-protest-turkey-media-crackdown-in-istanbul--27a95780964e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-thousands-protest-turkey-media-crackdown-in-istanbul" /><summary type="html">Several thousand people marched through Istanbul on Sunday to protest a growing crackdown on opposition and independent media outlets days after police raided pro-opposition broadcaster Sozcu TV, installing a government-appointed trustee and arresting senior staff members.</summary></entry><entry><title>Papers discuss James Bond's soft power and the next Bond girl</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7d063ed454db9a587be995a0ccd620dd9e819fc81b5720d1ea8b53e70cc9d72</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261123-papers-discuss-james-bond-s-soft-power-and-the-next-bond-girl--47aa511e9607.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261123-papers-discuss-james-bond-s-soft-power-and-the-next-bond-girl" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, November 23: Papers react to the breakdown of the COP31 climate talks. Israeli paper Haaretz reports on the struggles of crossing the Qalandiyah checkpoint. The New York Times talks about the mathematical "formula to stop the apocalypse". Finally, the Bond universe keeps making headlines.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian drones sink Russian warship at naval base in Libya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:87ee03aaa414714526d55c5bb35aae53c6b89d62e53ac2ed9c43489410a1e81c</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-ukrainian-drones-sink-russian-warship-at-naval-base-in-libya--063d86777c31.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-ukrainian-drones-sink-russian-warship-at-naval-base-in-libya" /><summary type="html">Ukraine carried out an attack on a Russian warship moored at a port in Libya, President Volodymyr Zelensky said Monday, claiming that sea drones sank the navy vessel in a surprise assault the previous day. Ukrainian forces deployed seven domestically made sea drones in the operation, which struck what was one of Russia’s newest vessels, commissioned a year after Moscow launched the 2022 full-scale invasion of its neighbour.</summary></entry></feed>
